      "content": "It is completely understandable that the idea of \"fixing\" things feels patronizing when you're facing such concrete, crushing realities like debt. Sometimes, the most immediate need isn't a grand solution, but just a break from the constant fighting. Could you consider finding one small, low-pressure point of contact, like a free financial counseling service, just to look at the numbers without the pressure to solve everything immediately?",
      "source": "target",
